---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import GuideTable from '../../components/GuideTable.astro';
import { MONTHS } from '../../lib/data';

const ALL = MONTHS.map((_, i) => i);
const rows = [
  { slug: 'cabo-san-lucas', label: 'Cabo San Lucas (Baja)' },
  { slug: 'puerto-vallarta', label: 'Puerto Vallarta (Pacific)' },
  { slug: 'mexico-city', label: 'Mexico City' },
  { slug: 'san-miguel-de-allende', label: 'San Miguel de Allende' },
  { slug: 'oaxaca', label: 'Oaxaca' },
  { slug: 'merida', label: 'Mérida (Yucatán)' },
  { slug: 'cancun', label: 'Cancún' },
  { slug: 'tulum', label: 'Tulum' },
  { slug: 'cozumel', label: 'Cozumel' },
];
---

<Guide slug="best-time-to-visit-mexico-by-region" photo="oaxaca">
  <p>
    The best time to visit most of Mexico is the dry season, from <strong>November to April</strong>: sunny beach days on both
    coasts and mild, clear weather in the highlands. From June to October the rainy season brings afternoon storms, and the
    Caribbean and Pacific coasts face hurricane risk, peaking in September. But Mexico's regions differ a lot — Baja is
    desert-dry, the Yucatán is hottest in spring, and the highlands are never too hot.
  </p>

  <h2>Weather rating by region and month</h2>
  <GuideTable caption="Weather rating in Mexico by region and month" months={ALL} rows={rows} />
  <h3>Rainfall</h3>
  <GuideTable caption="Average monthly rainfall in Mexico by region" months={ALL} show="rain" rows={rows} />
  <p class="small muted">Ratings combine average temperature and rainfall from national climate normals, with points off in hurricane season.</p>

  <h2>Region by region</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Baja California (Cabo San Lucas, La Paz):</b> sunny almost all year; December–April for whale watching (grey whales and humpbacks) and pleasant heat. Late summer is very hot, with a risk of Pacific hurricanes in September. See <a href="/destinations/cabo-san-lucas/">Cabo San Lucas</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Pacific coast (Puerto Vallarta, Oaxaca coast):</b> November–April is dry and sunny; June–October is hot, humid and wet. Humpback whales visit Banderas Bay from December to March. See <a href="/destinations/puerto-vallarta/">Puerto Vallarta</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Central highlands (Mexico City, San Miguel de Allende, Oaxaca city):</b> October–May is dry, sunny and mild; summer afternoons bring thunderstorms but mornings stay clear. Late October–early November is Día de los Muertos. See <a href="/guides/halloween-dia-de-muertos/">Día de los Muertos</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Yucatán and the Caribbean (Cancún, Tulum, Cozumel, Mérida):</b> December–April for beaches; April–May is very hot inland, sargassum can arrive from May to August, and September–October is the peak of hurricane season. See <a href="/best-time-to-visit-yucatan-peninsula/">the Yucatán Peninsula</a> and <a href="/guides/sargassum-season/">sargassum season</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Crowds and holidays</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Christmas–New Year</b> and <b>spring break</b> (March) are the busiest and priciest weeks in the beach resorts.</li>
    <li><b>Semana Santa</b> (Holy Week, March or April) is a national holiday — Mexican families fill beaches and colonial towns.</li>
    <li><b>Late April–June</b> and <b>November</b> are good-value shoulder months with mostly dry weather.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    See also: <a href="/best-time-to-visit-mexico/">the best time to visit Mexico</a> month by month and our guide to the{' '}
    <a href="/guides/rainy-season-mexico-central-america/">rainy season in Mexico and Central America</a>.
  </p>
</Guide>
